; sign-two.tasm — the same task using only TWO-WAY branches.
;
; A two-way branch is BR3 with two of its three arms pointing at the same place,
; which is exactly what a binary machine's conditional branch does. Note there is
; no spill: BR3 does not disturb the accumulator, so the second test reads the
; value still sitting in it. Charging this version a store/reload would be a
; strawman — the cost measured here is the branch structure and nothing else.
        IN
        BR3   t1
t1:     .table n, nn, nn      ; negative, or not
nn:     BR3   t2              ; not negative: zero, or positive
t2:     .table z, z, p
n:      LOADI -1
        JMP   e
z:      LOADI 0
        JMP   e
p:      LOADI 1
e:      OUT
        HALT
